","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed as Gerrit change 1679, merged to main as c18069c841 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1). Removed _RETIRED_GITATTRIBUTES_LINES, the strip arm, and the migration paragraph from the ensure-unit docstring; the gitattributes unit is now create-only. tests/interfaces/store/test_gitattributes_merge.py lost the C4 migration test; the drift matrix's gitattributes drift was retargeted from 'committed file carries the retired line' to 'no committed .gitattributes at all', which the surviving create arm reconverges. docs/release-notes.md carries the pre-1.0 pass #3 entry and CHANGELOG.md an Unreleased Removed bullet. Registry/tombstone treatment: NONE — this was internal store convergence, never a user-facing input, so it had no deprecation-registry row and takes no tombstone.","timestamp":1786569667878898001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CROSS-REFERENCE — provenance. This removal came out of the 2026-08-12 deprecation removal-readiness survey, which was originally written up on the LLM-gate cost-analysis ticket childsafe-bizarre-lorikeet (comment 11) — a scratchpad placement the operator has since ruled an anti-pattern. The survey summary now lives in session log cosey-vinegarish-mouflon (d0d8-9dfe-f2d8-4364), entry 2.\n\nWhat the survey said about this item: the ONLY Tier-1 \"ready to remove now, no policy conflict\" finding of the whole audit. The retired .gitattributes migration arm (src/rebar/_commands/init.py:600-616 plus _RETIRED_GITATTRIBUTES_LINES at init.py:69), introduced bbfa1c1d9b (2026-07-05). This store had already run it — git log origin/tickets -- .gitattributes shows exactly two commits, the second being 826d5ae379 \"drop retired .reconciler-* merge=ours\", and the live blob contains only \".bridge_state/* merge=ours\". ~15 LOC, one file, permanently unreachable here; the only residual risk noted was a clone that had not swept since 2026-07-05.","timestamp":1786588767795584001}],"created_at":1786566437368661001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d8354ffa-dad0-4623-98c4-e7e5a33e8e00","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b902-18af-14ed-4da1"},{"link_uuid":"6c336dce-bc3a-47a9-970d-95fa6ff8fb7c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3f8a-fc61-af62-4e7f"}],"description":"Operator-approved early removal (pre-1.0 breaking pass #3), 2026-08-12. Source: the DEPRECATION REMOVAL-READINESS SURVEY, comment #11 on childsafe-bizarre-lorikeet (b902-18af-14ed-4da1), Tier 1 item 1 — the only genuinely expired, genuinely dead surface found. Operator ruling (verbatim): \"The two best candidates and the one ready now are all approved for removal.\"\n\n## What\n\nDelete the dead `.gitattributes` migration arm that strips the retired `.reconciler-* merge=ours` line from an already-initialized tracker.\n\n## Why it is dead\n\nThe reconciler pass-lock/phase-gate moved onto `refs/reconciler/*` (epic dust-troth-naval / C4), so the union-merge carve-out was retired. This store ALREADY ran the strip: `git log origin/tickets -- .gitattributes` shows exactly two commits, the second being 826d5ae379 \"drop retired .reconciler-* merge=ours\", and the live blob contains only `.bridge_state/* merge=ours`. The arm is permanently unreachable here. Residual risk, accepted by the operator ruling: a clone that has not swept since 2026-07-05 would no longer be converged by `init`.\n\n## Scope (current main)\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/init.py:69` — the `_RETIRED_GITATTRIBUTES_LINES` constant and its explanatory comment.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/init.py:600-616` — the strip arm at the tail of the gitattributes ensure-unit; the unit then returns `EnsureOutcome(\"gitattributes\", \"ok\", \".gitattributes converged\")` for any existing committed `.gitattributes`.\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_gitattributes_merge.py:104-116` — `test_gitattributes_migration_strips_retired_reconciler_line`, which exercises only the deleted arm.\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_ensure_drift_matrix.py:25,88,106` — imports `_RETIRED_GITATTRIBUTES_LINES` and injects \"committed .gitattributes carries the retired line\" as the gitattributes drift; that drift is no longer convergent, so it is retargeted to the drift the surviving create arm still fixes (no committed `.gitattributes` at all).\n\nOut of scope: the gitattributes ensure-unit's create arm (School-B convergent, see `docs/migrations.md`), and the `.bridge_state/* merge=ours` line. No deprecation-registry or tombstone row is involved — this is internal store convergence, not a user-facing input, so it never had one.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `_RETIRED_GITATTRIBUTES_LINES` and the strip arm are gone from `src/rebar/_commands/init.py`; checked: `grep -rn _RETIRED_GITATTRIBUTES_LINES src tests` returns no matches.\n- [x] The ensure-unit reports converged for an existing `.gitattributes` and its create arm still writes the carve-out; proven by `pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_gitattributes_merge.py`.\n- [x] The drift matrix still converges every ensure unit with the gitattributes drift retargeted; proven by `pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_ensure_drift_matrix.py`.\n- [x] `docs/release-notes.md` carries a \"BREAKING (pre-1.0)\" entry for this removal recording \"operator-approved early removal (pre-1.0 pass #3), 2026-08-12\", following the format of the two prior passes (DE7 and the ticket-5899 sibling pass).\n- [x] Gates are green; checked: `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_gitattributes_merge.py tests/interfaces/store/test_ensure_drift_matrix.py` — the two suites that cover the ensure-unit's create arm and full-drift convergence.\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` — the commit gate.\n- `grep -rn _RETIRED_GITATTRIBUTES_LINES src tests` — proves the constant is fully gone (the LSP misses string-named references, so this is a raw grep per `docs/code-navigation.md`).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/init.py","reason":"delete _RETIRED_GITATTRIBUTES_LINES constant and the .gitattributes strip migration arm"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_gitattributes_merge.py","reason":"remove the C4 strip-migration test"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_ensure_drift_matrix.py","reason":"retarget the gitattributes drift injection (retired-line drift no longer exists) to the missing-file drift the create arm still handles"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"record the removal under the pre-1.0 breaking pass #3 window"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","3f8a-fc61-af62-4e7f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f1ab3c64-8083-4144-8b22-2219da68b9c5","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e654-58e2-0d38-48c6","ticket_type":"task","title":"Remove dead .reconciler-* gitattributes strip arm","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a6198d2d-5b0d-426f-b23c-9c4f083d5ec4","d8354ffa-dad0-4623-98c4-e7e5a33e8e00","b41fe083-b8e4-4f39-aa47-2a60124e22c7","b3a313c8-1dd1-4aae-b659-81bfe9f0bb03","abd76e40-9395-4ff0-82af-d04fad6303bb","7ab0eec0-9620-45c9-858f-02f8de8903b5","e81c69ba-7e27-4817-bdcc-9cbbf4835d9b","6c336dce-bc3a-47a9-970d-95fa6ff8fb7c","b6779081-b1f0-4b21-88e0-0eab9db04145","97a38917-a106-4ce8-9ae7-bb1712eb5d10","b629809b-8bf4-47e0-af80-d15581f2664e","e7cefe09-e80d-4fdf-b21a-a7486756598a","f1ab3c64-8083-4144-8b22-2219da68b9c5","34ebb1d7-3f59-45b0-8cff-e02accc9e012","8dc5deb8-ecb6-44d9-a471-8274751f7ed0"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786